    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 1; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nWhat is the average weight of the four men in kilograms? Martin's weight is 57 kg. Carl's weight is 18 kg more than Martin's weight. The comparison u...\n- {\"content\":\"Martin weighs \\\\(57\\\\) kg.\\n\\nCarl weighs:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n57+18=75\\\\text{ kg}\\n\\\\]\\n\\nLet the other two men weigh \\\\(x\\\\) kg and \\\\(y\\\\) kg. Then the average weight is\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{57+75+x+y}{4}\\n=\\\\frac{132+x+y}{4}\\n=33+\\\\frac{x+...",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Martin's weight is 55 kg.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Martin weighs \\(55\\) kg.\n\nCarl weighs:\n\n\\[\n55+18=73\\text{ kg}\n\\]\n\nIf the other two men weigh \\(x\\) kg and \\(y\\) kg, then the average is\n\n\\[\n\\frac{55+73+x+y}{4}\n=\\frac{128+x+y}{4}\n=32+\\frac{x+y}{4}.\n\\]\n\nSince the weights of the other two men are not given, the exact average cannot be determined.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{32+\\frac{x+y}{4}\\text{ kg}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Carl's weight is 16 kg more than Martin's weight.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Martin weighs \\(55\\) kg.\n\nCarl weighs:\n\n\\[\n55+16=71\\text{ kg}\n\\]\n\nIf the other two men weigh \\(x\\) kg and \\(y\\) kg, then the average weight is\n\n\\[\n\\frac{55+71+x+y}{4}\n=\\frac{126+x+y}{4}.\n\\]\n\nBecause the weights of the other two men are not provided, the exact average cannot be determined.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{126+x+y}{4}\\text{ kg}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Christian's weight is 8 kg more than Carl's weight.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Martin weighs \\(55\\) kg.\n\nCarl weighs:\n\n\\[\n55+16=71\\text{ kg}\n\\]\n\nChristian weighs:\n\n\\[\n71+8=79\\text{ kg}\n\\]\n\nLet the fourth man's weight be \\(x\\) kg. Then the average weight is\n\n\\[\n\\frac{55+71+79+x}{4}\n=\\frac{205+x}{4}\\text{ kg}.\n\\]\n\nSince the fourth man's weight is not given, the exact average cannot be determined.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{205+x}{4}\\text{ kg}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How much heavier is Christian than Martin?",
